# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF (two coupling subspaces), FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
# with ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO -- the NEO counterpart of lih_gnof_full_optimization.inp, same
# system, same functional. See water_muller_as_neo_full_optimization.inp for what
# ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO changes.
# PNOF/GNOF systems are where NEO's Newton trajectory has been observed (by comparison with the
# ADAM run) to occasionally converge to a DIFFERENT, nearby stationary point than ADAM's -- a
# genuine alternate solution of the coupled orbital+occupation problem, not a numerical error nor
# something a NEO iteration-budget setting fixes (both were checked). Compare against
# lih_gnof_full_optimization.inp's own converged energy as a routine cross-check.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
